Members of the two groups _have_ collaborated in the past to (quite!)
good effect, and both groups have benefitted from resources and
information made available by members of the othe group.

However, there are substantially different focuses between the two
groups.  One major (and, from the point of view of many NetBSD
developers and users, important) difference is that NetBSD will not
produce or use kernel code which is covered by the GPL, which rules
out using most Linux code...


